WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.838
The logins themselves move to
Entra principals, in parallel.

2
00:00:03.838 --> 00:00:07.698
People become Entra users,
ideally granted through groups,

3
00:00:07.698 --> 00:00:11.637
and they get phishing-resistant
MFA and Conditional Access.

4
00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:16.509
Groups become Entra group logins,
which SQL Server records as type X,

5
00:00:16.509 --> 00:00:20.337
with membership driven by
HR attributes from Book 03.

6
00:00:20.337 --> 00:00:24.025
Applications become service
principals and managed identities,

7
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:28.450
and the book is clear that Conditional
Access doesn't cover managed identities.

8
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.750
The migration is a parallel run.

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.825
Create the Entra user beside the Windows
user and copy its roles and permissions.

10
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:39.661
Keep both until the audit shows
no remaining Windows sessions,

11
00:00:39.661 --> 00:00:41.137
then disable the old one.

12
00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:46.724
Never convert in one step; and the old
runbook's shortcut, ALTER USER with LOGIN,

13
00:00:46.724 --> 00:00:51.175
only converts on Azure SQL Managed
Instance, not on SQL Server.

14
00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:56.073
One trap: the instance's Entra
administrator becomes sysadmin, and changing

15
00:00:56.073 --> 00:01:00.790
that administrator leaves the old
login as sysadmin until a DBA drops it.
